      "content": "That's a pretty strong stance. But some of our senior developers are pushing back, saying that focusing on outcomes instead of merit or individual effort will actually hurt our mathematical precision and undermine the whole point of an objective credit-scoring model. They think 'equality of opportunity' is the only way to keep things fair and actually data-driven. How would you respond to them?",
